This game is awesome! I'll try to keep this short.
130h in game, 58/59 achievements, one is not implemented;
This review is  about hardcore mode witch I prefer. Casual mode is much less challenging, the differences are clearly explain in the game. 
Facing off-road challenges using Russian trucks and tractors. You have few truck to use on a map, main task is to load a wood logs by a car with a crane, on to another cargo car, and deliver those to place marked on a map. You have to face deep mud, rivers, trees, lack of gasoline and damage taken by cars.
- the best mud I seen in computer game, it act like real!
- very good physics
- maps save your tracks, all tracks from all previously rides, so you can use only your tracks to navigate and no map or compass;
- you can get rid off compass by install 2017 HD mod (that mod dose not effect Steam achievements);
- awesome trucks, there is a reason why Russian are at the top positions in Dakar Race year by year;
- very relaxing I haven't suppose, good mix between relax and challenge in this game, you can play with beer in your hand, no police in Russian Taiga;
- you have to use your head a bit, do some strategy thinking, have a plan to approach a objectives;
- you can recover even from very bad situation, like truck turned upside down or when you stuck in a mud;
- you need wheel controller with force feedback to fully enjoy this game, Logitech G27 works fine;
- and manual gearbox;
- and xbox controller to load wood logs by a crane and control other options like camera movements;
- there is a guide how to set all this up;
- grate community, there is a lot of mods, trucks, maps, texture overhauls, etc.
- multiplayer is great but find some dedicated players to fill your lobby, lots of players disconnect from a game once they push themselves in trouble; occasionally trolls and no option to kick-out;
- game is good looking even on a old computers;
- I lost my saves in a crash once, so do the backup all the time, if you play long sp sessions;
- time consuming 12h for finish a map in SP HC, same game can take about 1h in MP with experience players, you can lost time tracking very easily;
- some players complain about camera in this game, well cam not working like in other games, is very specific; I'm switching cams by left keys on my G27 wheel controller and using D pad  pluse xbox controller to move and zoom, I have no trouble with it and is not that bad, as you may think after reading some reviews here;
- hud, I hate it, I wish to have switch off button for it;
- no cabin view only top of the roof view; there is a mod for it;
- no TrackIR support;
- no possibility to build things, like bridges, jumps or river dames, however there is an editor for map build, and a custom map with log bridge build option;
- no AI players, no life, limited wildlife, only some birds jump off bushes when you hit a horn;
- winch, use it to get of the mud: click advanced - hover mouse cursor over your truck - grab front or rear circle from your bumpers and pull to the near tree; next turn a gear and use winch, all together in the same time; just remember to stay close to trees when approaching deep mud;
- you can switch winch option from active to pull mode;
- to load a truck with logs, spawn logs, load by crane in hardcore mode, save a load by going advanced - engine on - hover mouse over load, when you see green boxes click it; in casual mode just go to lumber point and click load from pop-up menu;
- you can pull vehicles using a winch, sometimes is a only way to go with a logs through the map;
- move you assets on a map, before you hit the main objective: set a cistern in some good point, do the recon, witch way you will take a load, decide short, medium or long logs, always keep C  or E model save, do not risk it;
- you can roll over vehicle by pushing it, using two other trucks, push, block brakes, use other one do the same;
- park your trailer before you detach, if you forgot use a crane to pull it up;
- model K tractor, can take you through a lot just drive very, very slow and move side to side like a fish, but it can roll over very easily, the centre of gravity is high;
- C models are very universal
- E useful but need lots of fuel
- A good for exploring
- B and C/ best to keep as cistern or just trailer keeper; you need to keep truck attach to a trailer if you wan access it load, fuel or car fixing parts;
Loads / Objective points
- short logs 5 = 2
- medium logs 4 = 4
- long logs 3 = 6
