Simply put, Star Crusade is a sublime iteration on the fast-paced, click-n-drag style of digital CCGs first popularized by Hearthstone. Do not let the negative reviews discourage you from hopping into the cockpit of the closest Gargoyle Bomber and taking Star Crusade out for a spin around the galaxy!
Star Crusade has plenty to offer both veteran CCG players and newcomers alike;
See you in the stars!

Doing repetitive things in interface takes up 30% of your time, only playable on smaller maps if you want to enjoy the game itself.Fun game, but the interface gets more and more annoying as you build your empire, because there are too many steps between things;
Still no convenient ship list manager, no way to automate planets, no way to automate starbases which gets really annoying on bigger maps (imagine unautomated workers in civ - you only want to manage them for important decisions, not all the game).
Too bad its pretty much like GalCiv2, fun concept, killed by horrible interface things.

My 3~4yo son loves it.
Pros:
- very charming characters and tons of them;
- Tons of things to do, the main hub is huge and you can travel between separatist and republic ships;
- Codes to unlock new characters, so you don't have to play the whole thing, tho it's really fun to get the mini-kits and see the kids excitement for the new character.
Cons:
- The game isn't intuitive at all, actually, it's counter intuitive, be prepared to check guides and stare to the screen for a while to find out what you have to do;
- The split screen is great to play with the kids, tho it can get messy with you need to hit targets that are too far away;
- Jedis are overpowered and I hate to play with non-jedi toons.
The main problem is that the game is counter intuitive, but I have heard that most of lego games are like that. Otherwise is really amusing!

