This is a Great old classic in which you venture through a dungon to the lower levels, like the original diablo but the enermys will respawn :) which is great because diablo kinda let me down on lack of combat :). With the ability to use magic, be a barbarian or even a rouge with ranged weapons the possibilitys of different combat combinations are endless.
The whole pet system seemed odd at first but once you get use to it you will be feeding your dog or cat fish for days, turning them in to giant monsterous killing machines.
if your a classic rpg fan then this is for you :)

Top 2 things people are not happy about this game:
1. Optimisation;
2. Small variety of mission types.
I got this game much later than it was released, and i can say that optimisation is fixed already and the game plays extremely smooth on max settings for me (6700k, 1070, 2k monitor). I played a demo a lot earlier on the same PC, and i do see a huge difference in optimisation.
I played only few hours now, so missions variety is not an issue for me yet.
I`m actually writing my first ever review because i feel sorry that this game has mixed reviews and so underestimated :)
Why i consider this as a great game and a great Mafia 2 successor:
1. Stunning graphics;
2. Interesting characters and story;
3. I really like the driving physics. It`s less console like and it tries to simulate old cars. I just have fun with it;
4. Music;
5. Overall atmosphere of that time;
6. Many little touches and details of gameplay. For example when you ride on a mission and characters talk about something, after you hit a car or smth they will say something about an accident and then continue the misson talk starting with 'by the way' or 'as i was saying'. I know this might sound funny to someone, but because of that the game feels more real and more complete.
I just see and like how the devs really tried to make a great game, and i feel that they just didn`t had enougn time to do that before the release. But now, i do believe it is a great and fun game to play. And i enjoy it as much as i enjoyed Mafia 2.

