Easy on the beginning, extremely hard after clearing the Apprentice difficulty (the first 10 levels i guess), single player mode basically dead, sometimes even with a friend can be frustrating to finish a level, waaaaaaaay too much grind and a terrible "trap unlocking" and "upgrade" systems, sabotage is kinda good but it does not compensate for the rest of the game.
Major Problem (for me): The "trap unlocking" and "trap upgrade" systems - The systems are the same from Clash Royale, after finishing a level, depending on your score, you can get up to 2 chests, these chests can be Apprentice Chests (that contains only 2 types of trap duplicates and only duplicates of traps that are avaliable for you to unlock on the APPRENTICE difficulty), War Mage Chests (3 types of duplicates), and other chests from other difficulties wich contains more types of duplicates depending on the difficulty of the level that you got the chest and with more duplicates at some point you will be able to upgrade your trap, it sounds simple bou it's terrible, let me explain everything to you: You get chests depending on your score, but with "score" i mean "stars", for each level you can get up to 2 chests, one for 3 stars and 2 for five stars, to get the stars you must complete some objectives like "don't let you rift points drop below 75%" and the ridiculous "finish the level under 5 minutes (example)" wich is a terrible objective for new players because to get that star you need to use a strategy for the level to kill the orcs lightning fast, this means that you can't use the traps that you want and just shoot some orcs for fun and laugh at their faces (this is what killed this game for me ;-;), but let's say that you got the 5 stars and the 2 chests, you can get trap duplicates from common rarity to epic rarity but the traps that you can get works like the arena in clash royale, once you level up your arena (once you pass to a more difficult difficulty) you can get new card from the chests (you are able to collect new chests in wich you can get new duplicates from new traps), "but is they're the same systems, then why is the Orcs Must Die system that bad? Because you can get two and ONLY two chests per level, if you try the level again and get 5 stars again then the game will give you more skulls (common cash in the game) for getting 5 stars again, but in clash royale everytime that you have a chest slot empty you will get a chest after winning a battle, but in OMDU you won't get more chests for completing the levels, so there is the possibility that you can get stuck to the initial traps and not being able to upgrade them and (if you have a really bad luck) only recieve useless traps ond no duplicates for the traps that you actually use.
i didn't like this game and i think it's a shame that this game carries the name "orcs must die", more like "this game must die" RIP OMD ;-;

